[128.622855, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[4;2H\u001b[34m●\u001b[m The password-spraying source 198.51.100.22 is flagged in the threat-intel feed and got into svc_backup, a\r\n   backup operator account, on Nov 22 at 03:12. I'm moving on to the detection step now.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n \u001b[33m$\u001b[m \u001b[1mShell \u001b[mRun detection cell 20 lines…\r\n   cd /Users/Shared/splunk-demo/payments && jpterm execute hunt.ipynb --cell detection\r\n\r\n \u001b[34m●\u001b[m \u001b[1mFinding:\u001b[m \u001b[37m 198.51.100.22 \u001b[m is a confirmed, slow password spray. It has been active since Sep 07, hit       \r\n   333–335 accounts, and is a known spraying IP in the threat-intel feed. The old alert never saw it, since\r\n   its peak was 6 failures in 5 minutes against a threshold of 100. It \u001b[1mcompromised \u001b[37m svc_backup \u001b[39m (a backup \r\n\u001b[C\u001b[m  \u001b[1moperator) on Nov 22 at 03:12.\u001b[m             \r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   \u001b[1mNext steps, in priority order:\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[m\u001b[1K\r\n   1. \u001b[1mContain now.\u001b[m Reset \u001b[37m svc_backup \u001b[m's credentials, kill its sessions, and review what it did after 03:12\r\n\u001b[6Con Nov 22. Block \u001b["]
[128.622868, "o", "37m 198.51.100.22 \u001b[m at the edge.\r\n   2. \u001b[1mReview the other accounts.\u001b[m Force a password reset or MFA check on the roughly 335 targeted accounts,\r\n      starting with privileged ones.                                               \r\n   3. \u001b[1mDeploy the detection.\u001b[m The notebook's saved search flagged only this IP across 90 days, with no false\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K positives. Note that its SPL doesn't set a time range, so schedule it daily over a 24-hour window. I  \r\n      can create it with \u001b[37m splunkctl \u001b[m as \u001b[37m demo_password_spray_daily \u001b[m in the \u001b[37m search \u001b[m app. I'll show you the   ┃\r\r\n\u001b[6Ccommand first, as before.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   Do you want me to draft that saved-search command?                                 \r\u001b[6B \u001b[1m←\u001b[m open sidebar · Interactive · Manual Approval · \u001b[1m/\u001b[m commands · \u001b[1m?\u001b[m help · \u001b[1mtab\u001b[m next tab\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[143.622868, "o", "\u001b[?25l\r\n\r\n \u001b[1mctrl+c\u001b[m again to exit                                                               \u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
